<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Fencing in Richardson usually starts with a fence that is already there and tired. Many neighborhoods in this inner-ring suburb north of Dallas were laid out in the 1960s and 70s as ranch-house subdivisions, often with alleys behind the lots, and the wood fences along those alleys and side yards have lived through decades of North Texas storms. This page connects Richardson homeowners with independent fence contractors who quote the job. This site builds nothing itself.</p><p>Whether you are weighing repair against replacement, getting a fence back up after storm winds, or dealing with a driveway gate that quit, the honest approach is two or three comparable written quotes. <strong>Call now at (214) 555-0137</strong> and describe the job, or read the Richardson rules below first. Any price on this page is a figure a named firm publishes, never a quote from this site.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Richardson</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Richardson Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Wood privacy fence installation</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Cedar or pine, dog-ear or board-on-board, quoted by an independent contractor. The city of Richardson sets an 8 ft maximum along the rear and side, so settle the height before you compare quotes. See <a href="/fence-installation-dallas/">wood fence installation</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Fence repair</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Leaning sections, rotted posts and missing pickets are common on older alley and side-yard runs. Ask the contractor to say plainly whether the posts or only the boards have failed. See <a href="/fence-repair-dallas/">fence repair</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Gate repair and automatic gates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Sagging walk gates, failed latches and driveway openers that stopped moving. Power wiring for an opener is electrical work, so ask the installer who holds the electrical license. See <a href="/gate-repair-dallas/">gate repair</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Wrought iron fences</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Tubular steel and ornamental iron for front and side yards. Richardson's city page lists a 3 ft decorative limit forward of the front wall of the house, so check that before you fall for a tall front fence. See <a href="/iron-fence-dallas/">iron fences</a>.</p>
      </div>
</div>
